id: underwater-environment
name: Underwater Environment
kind: battlefield
environment: true
unbreathable: true
hardnessMin: 0
hardnessMax: 0
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Deep water. Unbreathable, so it wants a Survival Check on the way in and a stack of
  Held Breath a Round after that, and your Normal Speed is halved. Hardness Rank 0.
text: >
  Underwater Environment: A harsh environment where the water is deep enough to even
  submerge an Oozaru and where holding one's breath is a necessity for most.

  Hardness Rank: 0

  Effects: This Battle Environment has multiple effects:

  * This is an Unbreathable Environment.

  * While in this Battle Environment, halve your Normal Speed.

---

# "This is an Unbreathable Environment."
#
# Which settles something the Unbreathable rules left open: Unbreathable is a property an
# Environment has, not only an Environment of its own. `unbreathable: true` on the header
# is exactly that, and everything already reads it there - entering and leaving are watched
# by the same hook, the Survival Check is offered by the same button, the Combat Round and
# the Health Threshold take the same stack.
#
# So there is nothing to build here for it. The file says it is one and it is one, which is
# the whole point of having put that on a header rather than into a branch.
#
# --- Halve your Normal Speed ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Normal Speed, named outright - and it settles the Bog's "halve your Speed" while it is at
# it. The rulebook is careful about this: Tornado Weather says "your Speeds" and reaches
# both, the Bog says "your Speed", and this says "your Normal Speed". Three wordings, two
# of which are the same thing, and none of them accidental.
#
# So `speed.normal`, like the Bog. A character swimming can still Boost, which is the only
# way anybody crosses water at speed.
#
# --- Hardness Rank 0 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Features cannot have a Hardness value of 0, but the Squares themselves can" - and the
# surface of water is the entry's own example of Rank 0. Being thrown into deep water costs
# 1(bT) and nothing else. What it costs is not the landing.

[passive]
speed.normal *= 0.5;
